## Acceptance checklist
{{ acceptance }}

## DO
- Build every link at its WORLD rest pose to the plan's bbox (`check_contract`: max(10 mm, 10 %) per
  axis); one object named exactly as the link, with any helper objects parented under it (the
  wrapper joins them).
- Use the table's axes and limits (the skeleton already wrote them); if the motion check shows
  positive q moving the child against the plan's `motion` word, negate that axis — never swap the
  limits. `effort`/`velocity`: any positive numbers.
- Clearance is measured, not estimated: no overlap deeper than 2 mm in any sweep pose (a moved-pose
  overlap is always an ERROR; a rest overlap above 5 mm fails the build); a fixed child within 2 mm
  of its parent, a moving child within 10 mm.
- Every pivot lies on the real hinge line or slide axis of the part (the motion check measures the
  link's centroid displacement; a centred pivot gives none and the part sweeps through its neighbour).

## DON'T
- No camera/light/render/export calls in bpy; imports are the ones the blender lint allows (the
  contract's Allowed / forbidden section).
- No floating links: at rest a fixed child's mesh is within 2 mm of its parent's, a hinged or sliding
  child's within 10 mm (ERROR beyond 30 mm; a prismatic child already inside its parent's bbox is
  exempt).
- No joint whose child passes through another link anywhere in [lower, upper].
- No renaming of links/joints; no extra root links; one tree rooted at `{{ root_link }}` as planned.

